one in five of us is at risk of getting  liver disease  the British liver trust wants to see  universal screening introduced they say  the number of people dying from the  disease is now four hundred times higher  than forty years ago  Charlotte low-mass reports as a chef at  a michdan starred restaurant Alexei Gore  Tia likes to taste each dish before it's  served that was until he found out that  trying a little bit of everything was  enough to severely damage his health in  October 2010 he was diagnosed with liver  disease I thought there was something  wrong so interested doctor and and and  she was very surprised to see that I  have a liver problem and I was very  surprised too because what she described  was something that will happen to  someone who eat really a lot of drink a  lot which wasn't my case a lot in terms  of drinking but definitely in terms of  eating I didn't think I was overeating  in many areas of healthcare such as  heart disease death rates are going down  with liver disease it's the opposite  death rates have been soaring by four  hundred percent since nineteen seventy  is now the third most common cause of  early death among working aged people  health campaigners are calling for the  government to act and introduce liver  screening for everyone that's why MP  Luciana Berger put her liver to the test  on camera she joined a group of cross  party MPs lending support to the British  liver trust so I've just had my liver  tested and I'm delighted to find out  that I do have a healthy liver count  well finding out about liver disease  early actually saves the money to the  National Health Service because the  longer you wait and the longer and  people take to be diagnosed the higher  the cost can be people with liver  disease often don't show any symptoms  medical experts say Universal screening  will lead to earlier detection screening  would make a huge difference  my youngest patient with liver cirrhosis  secondary to obesity age 17 if she 